Phase 1 — Architecture Freeze

This is the most important phase of the project. Before writing a single line of implementation code, we'll finalize every architectural decision for the Product module.

Deliverables
Step 1.1 — Module Boundaries

Define the complete Product domain:

Catalog
├── Categories
├── Products
├── Brands
├── Collections
├── Tags
├── Attributes
├── Attribute Options
├── Variants
├── Inventory
├── Media
├── Pricing
├── Shipping
├── SEO
└── Product Listing

We'll also define ownership and interactions between these modules.

Step 1.2 — Folder Structure (Freeze)

Finalize the complete directory structure.

modules/
└── catalog/
    ├── shared/
    │   ├── constants/
    │   ├── lib/
    │   ├── validation/
    │   ├── dto/
    │   ├── mapper/
    │   ├── types/
    │   └── query/
    │
    ├── categories/
    ├── products/
    ├── brands/
    ├── collections/
    ├── attributes/
    ├── inventory/
    ├── media/
    └── pricing/

Each feature module will follow the same internal structure:

feature/
├── api/
├── dto/
├── hooks/
├── mapper/
├── repository/
│   ├── commands/
│   ├── queries/
│   └── index.ts
├── services/
├── validation/
├── constants.ts
├── keys.ts
├── types.ts
└── index.ts

This structure will remain fixed throughout implementation.

Step 1.3 — Execution Flow (Freeze)
UI Component
      │
React Query Hook
      │
Frontend API Client
      │
HTTP
      │
Next.js Route Handler
(Auth + Validation + Response)
      │
Domain Service
(Business Logic)
      │
Repository
(Database Access)
      │
Drizzle ORM
      │
PostgreSQL

No layer may bypass another.

